{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405999-challenging-your-players-with-demons-when-they-have-spirit-caging-mandala","id":1405999,"title":"Challenging your Players with Demons when they have Spirit-Caging Mandala","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-02T14:26:51-07:00","id":1405999,"title":"Challenging your Players with Demons when they have Spirit-Caging Mandala","content":"I'll just jump right into it (If play into in this group in Southren Denmark, don't read this.)<br /> <br /> So last session the group meet Octavian and a battle group of golems. The idea being the even the average Essence rating for the overall group is 3+ (four Solars and one Lunar), that Octavian would be a challenge for them<br /> <br /> Btw I have buffed Octavian with the ability to summon the equal of Lintha Reaver battle group size 3 and some terrestial sorcery spells.<br /> They start at long range from Octavian, with the golems between them.<br /> 1st or 2nd round the Twilight moves into medium range of Octavian and basically locks him down for 9 rounds, with the chance of doing it again reflexively for those rounds are over.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My question: The challenge was Octavian bashing them around, but now he is stuck for the rest of the battle. How do you work against Spirit-caging Mandala?<br /> <br /> Can the battlegroup try and throw the Twilight outside of medium range? Because at this point even if all the mentions had Smashing tag on their weapons, they are not getting past the Eclipse with melee defense charms, in fact at the moment they being slowly counter-attack to death.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have him summoning blood apes at the moment.<br /> <br /> Btw I read Spirit Caging Mandala as working within medium range of the target, certainly after it is activated, but I am willing to discuss that as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> BONUS QUESTION: If one or more of your players has this Charm, does that mean so can't challenge your players with one BIG Demon anymore? Or Mainly one BIG demon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","user":"light-hero","date":". 08-02-2020, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T21:16:35-07:00","id":1406052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405999-challenging-your-players-with-demons-when-they-have-spirit-caging-mandala#post1405999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question: The challenge was Octavian bashing them around, but now he is stuck for the rest of the battle. How do you work against Spirit-caging Mandala?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one big thing to consider is simply &quot;don't&quot;. Exalted has quite a lot of charms where the person with them will probably just win when they come up. Octavian should recognize Spirit-Caging Mandala (he's almost certainly had it used on him in the past, or heard of other demons who have), and will understand its limitations. He might well decide to, after he escapes the fight, to simply not battle the group unless he can arrange to do so when the Solar with S-CM isn't around. It's okay to have characters pull off these moments of awesome, where they get to show off their incredible might and flex on their opponents. All that said, there are some ways to deal with it in the fight where it happens, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the battlegroup try and throw the Twilight outside of medium range? </div> </div> </div> </div>I generally allow battlegroups that take the Engage action on individual characters to then move them around, as per the grappling rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[snip]<br /> they are not getting past the Eclipse with melee defense charms, </div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow Octavian to issue command actions to his battlegroup, which can significantly boost their dice pools. S-CM locks him in place, but doesn't prevent him from talking (or, in this case, shouting orders). He's got a Command pool of 8 dice, which should be a reasonably consistent 4 extra dice for the battlegroup's attacks. <br /> <br /> Besides command actions, remember that spirits trapped in S-CM can still make ranged attacks. Octavian can perform Strength 10 feats of strength. Consider allowing him to pick up a handy boulder or something like that and just hurl it at someone. His pool may not be as good, but it probably won't be completely terrible, either, and it can put more pressure on. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw I read Spirit Caging Mandala as working within medium range of the target, certainly after it is activated, but I am willing to discuss that as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said in the Ask a Question thread, I think S-CM is supposed to be Short range, because a) that's more balanced, and b) it says it's specifically inverting Spirit-Repelling Diagram, which only works out to Short range.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">BONUS QUESTION: If one or more of your players has this Charm, does that mean so can't challenge your players with one BIG Demon anymore? Or Mainly one BIG demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means that the big demon needs to have one of a few options:<br /> 1) Ranged attacks.<br /> 2) Ways to force the character maintaining the Mandala to move, which can include things like being able to throw down environmental hazards or spells, or <br /> 3) Other allies in the fight who aren't vulnerable to the charm, who can attack people in the area and still benefit from the spirit's abilities and charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T21:40:12-07:00","id":1406057,"title":"","content":"So, Octavian is facing off against 4 Solars and 1 Lunar, supported by a battlegroup of golems and his own ability to summon mooks. They Twilight has gotten in a decisive win, by rolling what I can only assume is 15 successes on a roll to trap him with Spirit-Caging Mandala, so now he's rooted in place long range from most of the party.<br /> <br /> You've already gotten the idea to use smashing attacks to move the Twilight out of range so the Charm ends. That's a good idea. You've got an Eclipse playing bodyguard at the moment, so having the golems punch the Twilight is out of the question. Let's see what other options are left to you.<br /> <br /> You could have Octavian summon Damaskenos, his Agata steed. It's a beefed up Agata strong enough to bear Octavian aloft, so you could have him summon it and send it to fly over the Eclipse and pick up the Twilight and carry him bodily away from the mandala. Alternatively, Damaskenos could just charge in and start fighting. A foe with an Initiative track isn't something you can just scoff at.<br /> <br /> Also, Octavian has tons of things he can do. He could use his magic acorn to summon all manner of earth elemental and intimidate them into attacking the party. He could wrench up chunks of the ground and throw them at the party as improvised ranged attacks, or use Mountain-Breaking Roar to target foes out to long range who strike at him. Also, with Devil Thews Exertion and Infernal Might Unleashed, he can get like 17 successes for free on Feat of Strength rolls, which is probably enough to rip open fissures in the earth that the whole party (Twilight included) have to roll to avoid falling into.<br /> <br /> A player having Spirit-Caging Mandala doesn't make them blanket immune to BIG Demons whatsoever. All it does is root Demons in place, which can be pretty effective when the party wants to harry them with ranged attacks, but if they want to stand and fight then the demon in question has all the advantages. The party has to come to them, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> What are your player trying to accomplish in this battle? What is Octavian trying to accomplish?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T06:38:04-07:00","id":1406623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405999-challenging-your-players-with-demons-when-they-have-spirit-caging-mandala?p=1406057#post1406057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... What are your player trying to accomplish in this battle? What is Octavian trying to accomplish?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are trying to get past the room he is guarding. A very old Solar has bound Octavian to guard they room and its entrance to level further down. <br /> <br /> Thank for the advice. Next step of the battle is tonight. <br /> <br /> Btw as we understand the Charm Octavian can't do anything to directly target the Twilight. But he can use work-arounds, like summoning Battle Groups and telling them to help him with his oath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T07:00:30-07:00","id":1406628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405999-challenging-your-players-with-demons-when-they-have-spirit-caging-mandala?p=1406623#post1406623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are trying to get past the room he is guarding. A very old Solar has bound Octavian to guard they room and its entrance to level further down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the old Solar need the entrance that Octavian's guarding to remain intact? A little bit of demolition could really shake things up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T10:20:42-07:00","id":1406644,"title":"","content":"Yeah a slight problem with Solars is that when they are against a challenge that involves their Supernal they just kinda auto-win. Which is, like, <i>the point</i>, but it can make challenging them quite tricky without resorting to <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/KryptoniteIsEverywhere\" target=\"_blank\">Kryptonite is Everywhere</a> scenarios or scenarios where players find themselves constantly asked to do the one thing their solar sucks at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T12:43:14-07:00","id":1406658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405999-challenging-your-players-with-demons-when-they-have-spirit-caging-mandala?p=1406623#post1406623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw as we understand the Charm Octavian can't do anything to directly target the Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not unless the Twilight attacks him first but anyone who does (Twilight included) is fair game for ranged attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T18:26:50-07:00","id":1407060,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice and the interesting inputs.<br /> <br /> btw my players kicked Octavian's ass. But lucky enough for me one for them killed hit him before the twilight could eat him and gain his powers. I ruled the killing let loose of the circle and sent him back to Malfeas.<br /> <br /> Demons returning to Hell is another thing I am a bit iffy one, so this time I just used hand-wavevium. But that is for another thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T20:22:43-07:00","id":1407072,"title":"","content":"The only handwavium is that it takes however long you feel like to happen. He could stay dead for a few days first, for a month, for a decade, you don\u2019t even really have to decide unless they want to pull an awkward and summon him themselves later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T06:23:09-07:00","id":1409886,"title":"","content":"For anyone else wondering about this. Robert Vance said it would be medium distance<br /> <br /> Here is the Thread Page from Ask the Devs 2<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page247\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page247\"> Ask the Devs v2 - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page247\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page247 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> It seems that, in my hubris, I've let the original Ask the Devs thread get a bit too long. If y'all wouldn't mind posting any new questions here. Thread rules </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}